Firox Linux screen savers (Settings > Screen Saver, `firox-screensaver`).

Each NAME.conf is one screen saver:

    NAME=Aquarium                 shown in the list
    COMMAND=asciiquarium          run full screen in a black terminal
    TERMINAL=false                optional: COMMAND opens its own window
                                  (make it full screen yourself)

Add your own in ~/.local/share/firox/screensavers/ (just for you) or
/etc/firox/screensavers/ (everyone). A file with the same name as one here
replaces it. Any terminal program works, e.g. one installed with brew or in a
toolbox, as long as the command can be run from a terminal.
